PR2 of the four-PR closure sequence for INV-fibis / INV-nuhun.

kotlin and javascript emit NO call edge for an external instance-method call
(WI-nasuf), so the untyped-receiver disclosure PR1 made reachable has nothing
to hang on for them: it discloses an edge the analysis EMITTED and could not
adjudicate, and here no edge exists. A clean verdict came out a bare
`confirmed` over 232 catalogued method-kind sinks -- kotlin 181 of its 186
primitives (97%), javascript 51 of 187.

THE FACT IS DECLARED, NOT INFERRED, because the edge set cannot express it.
"this repository contains no external method calls" and "this analyzer never
emits them" produce the SAME EMPTY SET and opposite verdicts. So
analyzer_disclosure.py carries a dated per-language declaration with the
measurement behind it, and emits_external_method_call_edges FAILS CLOSED --
an undeclared language answers False and is treated as blind until somebody
measures it. A test turns that default into a hard gate.

NOT IN io_primitives/*.yaml, deliberately: those catalogue what a LIBRARY
does; this records what an ANALYZER can see.

A CAVEAT, NOT A WITHHOLD. Those analyzers do emit call edges, just not this
shape, so "I examined everything I could see, except this whole construct" is
the true sentence and is a qualified opinion (ADR-0016 section 4);
`inconclusive` would claim the analysis formed no view at all. It rides BOTH
the boundary and taint arms, because a run that discloses on one and stays
silent on the other about the same unseen call is the asymmetry INV-nuhun
names.

Measured at the published-output layer, with a falsifiability control:
  kotlin, clean  -> confirmed_with_caveats rc 3, "kotlin (181 of 186
                    catalogued primitives are method-kind). Declared
                    2026-08-23."
  go, clean      -> BARE confirmed rc 0        <- not a blanket downgrade
  kotlin, taint  -> the same caveat on every taint verdict

ONE EXISTING TEST PINNED THE OLD SILENCE and was changed rather than relaxed:
test_verify_claims_covered_languages_confirm asserted a clean bare confirm
over a python+javascript map. Its CONTRACT -- a clean verdict over SIGHTED
languages stays bare -- is still right and is preserved by swapping javascript
for go; relaxing it to accept rc 3 would have destroyed exactly what it
tests. The javascript side is pinned from the other direction in
test_declared_analyzer_blindness.py.

The declaration flips to True when WI-nasuf builds the missing edges, and the
caveat stops firing with no invariant changing colour -- which is the reason
the owner rewrote the bar (LIVE.md rule 19).

